+/**
+ * Applies the escalation calendar to a single unit.
+ *
+ * The calendar is a property of the UNIT, not of the deployment that happens to
+ * field it, because the same deployment data is shared by every generated Cobra
+ * site. Writing the dates into the deployments would mean maintaining the same
+ * calendar in eight places and still getting it wrong for a scripted mission.
+ *
+ * Three parts, as the design has it:
+ *
+ *   earliest  a hard floor. Never before this, whatever Cobra's books say.
+ *   full      by this month it turns out at full strength; between the two it
+ *             ramps, and a well-supplied region gets there faster. That is the
+ *             "organic" half - Cobra's own state decides when inside the window.
+ *   latest    a ceiling, so a unit can be withdrawn as the war moves on.
+ *
+ * missionOnly is the separate rule that B.A.T.s needed. CLAUDE.md: B.A.T.s in
+ * months 4-22 "belong to named missions only". So a unit flagged this way may
+ * be fielded OUTSIDE its window, but only by a deployment that names it
+ * outright - a scripted mission - never by a generic garrison. Set alongside
+ * earliest 22 that reads exactly as the calendar does.
