+/**
+ * Turns a finished research topic into LEADS on the globe.
+ *
+ * Spine row 19 is "reveals hidden Terror Dromes on the globe", and the design
+ * is careful that intel is not the same thing as knowing: the player learns a
+ * Drome is out there and roughly where, not its doorstep. So this does NOT
+ * call AlienBase::setDiscovered - the site stays hidden and its own marker
+ * stays off - and instead drops a GlobeMark with fromIntel set.
+ *
+ * That flag is the whole point. Globe::drawMarks already ages an intel mark
+ * down a confidence tier once it is MARK_STALE_MONTHS old, while a pin the
+ * player placed himself never decays, because he is not guessing about his own
+ * guess. Until this existed nothing in the game ever set fromIntel, so the
+ * situation board had a confidence ladder with only the player's own rungs on
+ * it.
+ *
